 "narration": [
  "That bag of cement has a carbon footprint. An EPD is how you read it.",
  "EPD stands for Environmental Product Declaration. Think of it as a nutrition label for a building product.",
  "It reports the product's impacts, like its carbon, measured with a life cycle assessment.",
  "For construction products it follows EN 15804, and it's checked by an independent verifier before it's published.",
  "Most EPDs are valid for five years. Always check the date, and the declared unit: per kilo, per square metre or per cubic metre.",
  "Why it matters: LEED rewards products with EPDs, and whole-building LCA tools use them as their data.",
  "So next time a supplier says low carbon, ask one thing. Can I see the EPD?"
 ],
